A||||6||JAMIE||How often to start up.||||1||
Z||000000||JAMIE||05-26-2000||09:18 AM||||My Fieros sit for long periods of time between usage and are stored from October to May.How often should I start the cars and for how long should I let them run. Any rule of thumb?||||reg||1
Z||000001||rogergarrison||05-26-2000||10:42 AM||||Im a firm believer in driving a car AT LEAST 1/2 hour every 2 weeks. Letting it just idle is no good for anything else but the motor. It has to drive long enough to heat and burn off condensation in engine and exhaust. If you dont youll have problems, like dried up seals in trans, corrosion in cooling system, locked brakes, flat spotted tires, just to name a few.<BR> <BR>rg||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||05-26-2000||10:42 AM||||Im a firm believer in driving a car AT LEAST 1/2 hour every 2 weeks. Letting it just idle is no good for anything else but the motor. It has to drive long enough to heat and burn off condensation in engine and exhaust. If you dont youll have problems, like dried up seals in trans, corrosion in cooling system, locked brakes, flat spotted tires, just to name a few.<BR> <BR>rg||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||05-26-2000||11:04 PM||||I second that. Let it come up to temperature and drive it.||||reg||1
Z||000004||fierodave||05-27-2000||06:37 AM||||Unless of course you live in an area like Jamie does and won't winter drive his future show car!<BR>Jamie I store mine in the winter here in WI. like this----  i put it up on jack stands with the tires just touching the ground&lt; you don't want the full load off the suspension a little is good!  and the tires should not flat spot this way. besides you can once a month rotate each tire 1/4 turn if your worried about it!<BR>I start mine once every two weeks and let it come up to operating temp,<BR>I then jack it up off the ground and let it run in third gear for about 10 minutes. <BR>Then I tap the brakes a few times to use them too!  and shut off the car  put it back down at the right leval off the floor, set and reset the e-brakes about a dozen times, and go home  I do keep the tank as full as possible before storing it, and also add a bottle of fuel line treatment to the car.<BR>This should keep all the seals mentioned moist.  ALSO  don't forget to run the AC for at least 5 minutes every two weeks to keep that in good shape too!<BR>FD ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Gokart||05-27-2000||06:58 AM|||| <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20000503-2-001194.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Archives/Archive-000001/HTML/20000503-2-001194.html</A> ||||reg||2
Z||000006||batboy||05-27-2000||10:13 AM||||If you live in a cold climate, consider removing the battery and storing it where it doesn't drop below freezing. Put it on the charger at least once a month too.||||reg||1
